# Round 18, C1-6 (follows). L §3.3 defines factor(r, n, P, c) with the compounding required (P-14: nothing defaults
# it); L §2.3's example is now factor(i, 1, year, effective). A call with three arguments is refused.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
input i: rate
def f3: num = factor(i, 1, year)
version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  i = 5 %/year
ask q: f3
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: factor takes 4 arguments ...
